# AI Board NAT Controller — general configuration v0.4.0 (development)
# MODE: DISABLED removes managed rules; AUDIT reports drift without
# changing existing rules; ENFORCE installs and repairs desired rules.
# EXPECTED_WAN_IP: primary WAN IPv4 address, not an additional IP.
# A mismatch blocks audit/enforcement; DISABLED cleanup bypasses WAN checks.
# MODE and EXPECTED_WAN_IP mandatory; case-sensitive KEY=VALUE, no spaces.
# DNAT_ALLOWED_INTERFACES: optional with no enabled DNAT; required for
# enabled DNAT. Comma-separated interface names, no
# duplicates, maximum 32. Only explicitly authorised LAN/VLAN interfaces.
# Route and local-address validation must also pass; never list WAN or
# management interfaces. Omission grants no DNAT destination permissions.
# DNAT_RUNTIME_POLICY: optional, default WITHDRAW_UNSAFE.
# PRESERVE: retain installed rules on runtime destination failures.
# WITHDRAW_UNSAFE: withdraw only mappings with confirmed unsafe destinations.
# WITHDRAW_UNVERIFIED: also withdraw mappings whose safety cannot be verified.
# Applies to installed mappings in ENFORCE; AUDIT never writes.
# All proposed mappings must still pass destination validation; Force is
# independent. Existing conntrack entries may survive withdrawal.
# Development: policy parsing/classification only until integration.
# Blank lines and full-line # comments accepted; no inline comments.
# Invalid configuration leaves existing rules in place.
# Replace atomically using a sibling .new file and mv.
# Documentation address below MUST be replaced locally.
MODE=AUDIT
EXPECTED_WAN_IP=203.0.113.10

DNAT_ALLOWED_INTERFACES=br0

DNAT_RUNTIME_POLICY=WITHDRAW_UNSAFE
